'''Grindalids''' were a [[Annelid/Canon|annelid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] native to [[Persis IX]], an [[Expansion Region]] planet with a dense [[atmosphere]] that blocked out the light of its [[star]]. As such, they had photosensitive skin that caused them to burn very easily when exposed to sunlight. [[Lady]] [[Proxima]] led the [[White Worms]] on [[Corellia]] during the [[Imperial Era]], alongside fellow Grindalids [[Moloch]] and [[Jabbat]]. [[Han Solo]] later exploited her vulnerability to light in order to escape the [[Den of the White Worms|lair]].

==Biology and appearance==
{{Quote|How many bracelets did you make?!''"<br />"''Proxima has a lot of arms!|[[Sana Starros]] and [[Doctor]] [[Chelli Lona Aphra]]|<ref name="Doctor Aphra (2020) 7">[[Doctor Aphra (2020) 7|''Doctor Aphra'' (2020) 7]]</ref>}}
[[File:Moloch-SoloTOC.png|thumb|left|180px|Grindalids appeared humanoid when wearing protective armor.]]
[[Sentience|Sentient]] [[Annelid/Canon|annelids]]<ref name="Star Wars: Scum and Villainy" /> with similarities to [[worm]]<ref name="Solo" /> and [[insect]] [[species]],<ref name="Alien Archive">''[[Star Wars: Alien Archive]]''</ref> Grindalids were native to [[Persis IX]],<ref name="Galactic Explorer's Guide" /> a [[homeworld]] with a dense [[atmosphere]] that rendered them light-adverse. Because of this, their squinting,<ref name="Official Guide" /> sensitive [[eye]]s were easily damaged on lighter worlds,<ref name="Alien Archive" /> and their photosensitive skin burned and blistered when exposed to direct [[Star|sunlight]].<ref name="Solo" /> Prolonged exposure to sunlight caused a Grindalid to disintegrate into dust upon [[death]].<ref name="Midnight Horizon">''[[The High Republic: Midnight Horizon]]''</ref> Some wore protective [[clothing]] when outside, consisting of articulated faceplates, flexible cowl [[armor]], long coats, [[glove]]s, and full-seal armored coverings.<ref name="Official Guide" />

Grindalids hatched from [[egg]]s and lived in [[water]]y pools as [[Youngling|youngsters]]. They had pale faces, squinting eyes, and large, curved heads. While seemingly [[humanoid]] in appearance while wearing armored coverings, Grindalids had tapered tail segments in place of [[Limb|legs]]. Some were capable of impersonating a humanoid walk through extensive practice.<ref name="Official Guide" /> Grindalids possessed two primary, if stubby, arms, with many more pairs of shorter pincers running the length of their wrinkled, serpentine bodies.<ref name="Alien Archive" /> They were capable of living for long periods of time of up to over two hundred [[Standard year|years]].<ref name="Midnight Horizon" />

[[Gender|Females]] fed and cared for young hatchlings in filmy watery pools, chewing up morsels of meat to feed to their baby worms. Grindalids were [[Diet|carnivores]], eating vermin like [[vervikk]]s and [[screerat]]s.<ref name="Official Guide" />

==Society and culture==
[[File:Moloch.png|thumb|right|200px|Moloch wearing his mask]]
Some Grindalids were spiritual: [[Moloch]] believed in the promise of an afterlife with endless riches.<ref name="Official Guide" /> Others adorned their bodies with trinkets and jewels: [[Proxima]] wore plates and rings down the length of her back.<ref name="Alien Archive" />

In Grindalid culture, it was custom for a Grindalid to eat those who murdered a Grindalid. If the culprit was not found, the next being held responsible would be devoured instead.<ref name="Midnight Horizon" />

==Grindalids in the galaxy==
[[File:DenOfTheWhiteWorms-Databank.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Grindalids Moloch (left) and Proxima (right) with scrumrats (center)]]
During the [[High Republic Era]], the [[Garavult Clan]], a group of thousands of Grindalids led by Mother [[Fastidima]], worked alongside the [[City Father]]s, protecting the sewers and tunnels of [[Coronet City]], on the planet [[Corellia]].<ref name="Midnight Horizon" />

Following the [[Proclamation of the New Order|fall]] of the [[Galactic Republic|Republic]], several members of the species formed the [[White Worms]],<ref name="Alien Archive" /> a gang of [[scrumrat]]s in the slums of the city. The gang was led by the Grindalid [[Crime lord|crime lady]] Proxima from her [[Den of the White Worms|Den]], assisted by Moloch. She issued orders from the watery pool in which she resided with her young hatchlings.<ref name="Official Guide" />

